 "notes": {
  "forAnalyst": "Operational telemetry in Azure Monitor: requests, dependencies, failures and traces from a running instance.",
  "forArchitect": "No dependencies, three settings, no schema — configuration that turns on the Azure SDK. Xapi even registers a telemetry processor to keep plain GraphQL POSTs from flooding it, which tells you how much traffic this sees.",
  "forDeveloper": "Sampling and cost are the design decisions. Correlate by operation id across hosts; without that a scaled-out deployment produces telemetry you cannot join.",
  "owns": [],
  "reachForItWhen": [
   "You need to see what a deployed instance is doing",
   "An incident needs traces or metrics that survive a restart",
   "The hosting platform already collects this format"
  ],
  "doNotReachForItWhen": [
   "Business reporting — this is operational telemetry, not analytics",
   "You want an audit trail of who changed what: that is Audit Log",
   "Adding several collectors for the same signal, which doubles cost for one answer"
  ]
